{
  "note": "Here is a guide to your weak areas with hints to help you remember Tarnball's tricky 'anti-intuition' rules!\n\n1. OUT OF BOUNDS: The team that touched it last gets it back. \nHINT: 'Losers Keepers' - if you knock it out, you keep it!\n\n2. SCORING TIMING: Goals in the last 60 seconds count double ONLY for the trailing team. \nHINT: 'Underdog Minute' - only the team behind gets the catch-up multiplier.\n\n3. FOUL ACCUMULATION: A player's 3rd foul sends off their CAPTAIN, not the player. \nHINT: 'The captain goes down with the ship.'\n\n4. POSSESSION PENALTIES: Holding the ball for >5 seconds gives the opponent a free throw, but NOT possession. \nHINT: 'Keep the ball, give a throw' - you get penalized but retain possession.\n\n5. LEAGUE STANDINGS: A tiebreak LOSS earns 2 points, while a tiebreak WIN earns 1. If tied on table points, FEWER goals scored ranks higher. \nHINT: 'Tarnball is Golf' - losing the tiebreak is better for points, and fewer goals wins the standings tie.\n\n6. CHALLENGES: An unsuccessful challenge costs the team 1 point. \nHINT: 'Put your score where your mouth is!' Bad challenges literally subtract from your scoreboard.\n\nHere is your next practice set mixing these concepts:",
